cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these building blocks in research, please cite this software."
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/noelEOS/tensor-ee"
title: "TensorEE: PyTorch-compatible neural-network building blocks for Earth Engine"
authors:
  - family-names: Ulloa
    given-names: Noel Ivan
# Concept DOI: resolves to the latest archived release on Zenodo.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23524569
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Experimental building blocks that run pretrained PyTorch models natively in
  Google Earth Engine, as Earth Engine raster and array operations with no
  model-serving endpoint. A restricted CNN compiler translates the SegWater
  ResNet18 U-Net and standard segmentation-models-pytorch Unet and UnetPlusPlus
  models on ResNet and VGG encoders, a converter maps supported attention models (SMP SegFormer-B0,
  and SMP UPerNet with timm's Swin-T) onto the library's blocks, and a planner
  and runner split their graphs into staged exports.
